Not affiliated with Samsung
---------------------------

This is an unofficial, independent client that is compatible with Samsung
Notes and Samsung Cloud. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
sponsored by Samsung Electronics Co., Ltd. "Samsung", "Samsung Notes",
"Samsung Cloud" and "Galaxy" are trademarks of Samsung Electronics Co.,
Ltd.; they are used here only to describe compatibility. The file formats
and protocol were documented through interoperability analysis (network
observation, file inspection and static analysis of the official clients);
the project contains no Samsung code, binaries or assets.


sdocx (ink-render CLI and live pen preview)
-------------------------------------------

tools/ink-renderer builds the separate `ink-render` command-line program and
crates/notes-ink-live builds the live pen preview WebAssembly module; both
statically link the sdocx crate:

  Project:  sdocx - https://github.com/twangodev/sdocx
  Commit:   41e9c1099b29a48dc7320501573d7c4858f09303
  License:  GNU General Public License v3.0 only (LICENSE in that repository)

Our own code is GPL-3.0-or-later, but sdocx is licensed GPL-3.0-only, so the
ink-render and notes-ink-live binaries are distributed under GPL-3.0-only as
a whole.

sdocx is not vendored in this repository. Builds fetch it at the pinned
commit into references/upstream/sdocx, and tools/ink-renderer/build.rs
verifies that checkout before compiling. The application talks to
ink-render only over pipes. Binary releases that include ink-render ship its
Corresponding Source (tools/ink-renderer plus sdocx at the commit above)
alongside the release assets.


Other third-party components
----------------------------

Rust crates and npm packages used by the engine, the desktop shell and the
UI are listed with their licenses in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md, generated by
tools/third_party_licenses.py from the lock files. All of them are under
GPL-3.0-compatible licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, ISC, Zlib, Unicode-3.0,
MPL-2.0, ...); deny.toml enforces that list for the Rust workspaces.

The UI icons (desktop/assets-free/windows-assets) are rendered from Lucide
(https://lucide.dev), ISC License, with portions derived from Feather (MIT
License); see desktop/assets-free/LICENSE.

The UI uses fonts installed on the system (Segoe UI if the user has it,
otherwise Noto Sans, Cantarell, Ubuntu, DejaVu Sans or the system default).
The page text editor also bundles unmodified Roboto fonts from
https://github.com/googlefonts/roboto (Apache License 2.0); the license is in
desktop/public/page-fonts/Roboto-LICENSE.txt.
No fonts are bundled.
